Provenance rescue (not in the commit message, which is about the artifact viewer):

This commit also carries an unrelated correctness fix in
nvidia/cmd/cudaprof/view_nvrtc.go -- the nvrtcx.WithNoCache() option on the
recompile path, and its comment. That fix is why the NVRTC flag comparison
panel reports honest numbers.

The defect: the nvrtcx content-addressed cache served CUBINs that no fresh
compile produces. Measured against NVRTC 13.0 on ds4_math.cu, fresh compiles
of base, --ftz=true, --prec-div=false, --prec-sqrt=false and
--extra-device-vectorization all yield CUBIN 7f5d5871d61abd48 (2305256 bytes),
reproducibly across separate processes -- those four flags are no-ops on that
source. Served from the cache, base gave 5f450e62 (2305232) and the four gave a
shared 05d18dcd (2338920), and the panel reported them removing 24 FCHK and 8
MUFU.RCP. The tell was four unrelated flags agreeing to the instruction.

A comparison that invents a difference is worse than a slow one, so every
variant on this path is compiled fresh. After the fix, --ftz=true honestly
shows 81 changed PTX opcodes (fma.rn.f32 1421->0, fma.rn.ftz.f32 0->1498) and
zero changed SASS rows.

